\section{Extension contract}{

A reader or writer is a function whose first argument is a file path (plus
\code{...}). An operation is any function, keyed by \code{name} and tagged with an
optional \code{modality} (e.g. \code{"eeg"}). Keys are matched case-insensitively and
with surrounding whitespace trimmed; the \verb{available*()} discovery tables
therefore report keys in their normalized (lower-cased) form. Registering a
key that already exists errors unless \code{overwrite = TRUE}. A typical consumer
registers in its \code{.onLoad} with \code{overwrite = TRUE}, which keeps registration
idempotent across dev reloads (\code{devtools::load_all}):

\if{html}{\out{<div class="sourceCode r">}}\preformatted{.onLoad <- function(libname, pkgname) \{
  PhysioExperiment::registerReader("brainvision", readBrainVision,
                             ext = c("vhdr", "eeg"), overwrite = TRUE)
\}
}\if{html}{\out{</div>}}

The store is anchored in a session option, so it survives a PhysioExperiment reload
and is shared across packages. Resolution is last-writer-wins: if two packages
register the same key with \code{overwrite = TRUE}, the one loaded later prevails;
\verb{available*()} shows which function is currently active.
